From 991c0953d708ef833e92bae5de75cc4ce183539a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: albanread <albanread@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 19:53:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] prose_display: no colour-bar test card by default

The kernel test pattern was milestone A scaffolding, from before the
accelerant existed: it proved the pipe by drawing colour bars and an
animated box from a kernel thread. With the accelerant driving the
display it only flashes for a moment during boot, and the host now shows
analogue static until the guest's first commit, so the bars interrupt
that rather than adding anything. PRDS_TEST_PATTERN 1 restores it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../kernel/drivers/graphics/prose_display/prose_display.cpp     | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/prose_display/prose_display.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/prose_display/prose_display.cpp
index 2ee1cdb250..c6b3410062 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/prose_display/prose_display.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/graphics/prose_display/prose_display.cpp
@@ -38,7 +38,7 @@
 
 #define PRDS_EVENT_BUFFERS		8
 #define PRDS_RESPONSE_OFFSET	2048	// in the command page
-#define PRDS_TEST_PATTERN		1		// milestone A: draw and animate ourselves
+#define PRDS_TEST_PATTERN		0		// the host shows TV static instead (hvgpu); 1 restores the self-test
 
 #define ALIGN_UP(x, a) ((((x) + (a) - 1) / (a)) * (a))
 
-- 
